Dammit, I hate it when people post riddle spoilers, especially when you
essentially *asked* to be spoiled.  Here's the answer plainly:

The only way to lose the intrinsic of teleportation, when it is
acquired from eating a monster, is to have it stolen by a gremlin after
midnight.  They can steal other intrinsics too (including Aggravate
Monster, which would be good, but also many other useful intrinsics),
so be careful.  Generally it's best not to gain it in the first place,
so next game try to avoid eating nymphs, leprechauns and tengu.

HOWEVER... since you have teleportitus anyway, you might as well make
the best of it.  Try to eat any tengu you can find, as to my knowledge
they are the only monster in the game that can bestow intrinsic
teleport control.  Ordinarily eating them carries a big risk of gaining
teleportation, but since you have it already you might as well try for
TC as well.

